I am in the process of ensuring that our company's legal documents comply with the latest data protection regulations. We have multiple documents including our service agreements, terms of service, and privacy policies that need a thorough review. Specifically, I am looking for clauses relating to how data is handled, retained, and what actions are required in the event of a data breach. Please extract these clauses from the below-listed documents using the `extract_legal_clauses` function:

- Service Agreement: [Service Agreement PDF](https://www.company.com/contracts/agreement1.pdf)
- Terms of Service: [Terms of Service PDF](https://www.company.com/contracts/terms_of_service.pdf)
- Privacy Policy: [Privacy Policy PDF](https://www.company.com/contracts/privacy_policy.pdf)

I am also interested in determining if these clauses meet the standard regulatory requirements provided in the following link: [Data Protection Standard Regulations](https://www.regulations.com/data_protection_standard.json)

Use the `compare_clauses_to_regulations` function to compare the extracted clauses against these standard regulatory requirements and inform me if they are compliant.

To assist with this task, please call the appropriate functions with the aforementioned documents and regulatory requirements. Here's how you could structure the JSON object for the `multi_tool_use.parallel` function call:

```json
{
  "tool_uses": [
    {
      "recipient_name": "functions.extract_legal_clauses",
      "parameters": {
        "documents": [
          "https://www.company.com/contracts/agreement1.pdf",
          "https://www.company.com/contracts/terms_of_service.pdf",
          "https://www.company.com/contracts/privacy_policy.pdf"
        ],
        "clause_types": [
          "data_handling",
          "data_retention",
          "data_breach_notification"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "recipient_name": "functions.compare_clauses_to_regulations",
      "parameters": {
        "extracted_clauses": "output_of_extract_legal_clauses",
        "regulatory_requirements": "https://www.regulations.com/data_protection_standard.json"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

The expected outcome is to receive feedback on each clause's compliance status to guide our next steps in amending the contracts if necessary.

I recently acquired an Android smartphone with the unique device ID "A1B2C3D4E5F6" and I'm interested in enabling the developer options to access advanced capabilities. Furthermore, I've installed the AccuWeather application, package name "com.accuweather.android", and I want to set the app's language to Spanish, "es". Lastly, I want to verify if system tracing is currently active on my device to ensure there's no unnecessary performance impact. Could you assist me by enabling the developer options, changing the AccuWeather app's language to Spanish, and checking the system tracing status on my device?

```json
{
  "enable_developer_options": {
    "device_id": "A1B2C3D4E5F6"
  },
  "change_app_language": {
    "app_package_name": "com.accuweather.android",
    "language_code": "es"
  },
  "check_system_tracing_status": {
    "device_id": "A1B2C3D4E5F6"
  }
}
```
